# Unchanged unmanifested draft context: explicit owner opt-in

This route handles a genuine native reader finding labelled `in-run-dependency` whose actual direct supplier is an own-run draft helper with **zero homes in every current run manifest**. It supplies read-only context to the already assigned consumer Alpha. It does not invent a producer batch, add a frontier item, broaden refuter coverage, adopt source reading, grant edit permission or accept mathematics.

Root registers `research/RUN-step3-owner-unmanifested-draft-context.json` with `{version:1,run,policy:"owner-step3-unchanged-unmanifested-draft-context-v1",authorized_by:"owner",authorization,contexts:[ENTRY]}`. Authorization is at least 40 characters. Nothing automatically writes this registry.

ENTRY fields:

- `version:1`, exact `run`, same `policy`, `owner_identity:"/root"`, `reviewed:true`, `mathematical_acceptance:false`, `edit_permission:false`, `coverage_adopted:false`.
- Actual `at` at or after successful native completion; concrete `reason` at least 80 characters. `batch` is the assigned consumer batch, `index` is the one-based original reader finding, `id` the helper, `consumer_id` the assigned consumer, and `finding_sha256` uses the existing exported `requiredPageHash` canonical JSON algorithm.
- Raw `{path,sha256}` own-run research references `findings` (immutable original complete findings JSON archive), `native_result` (exact original `reader-reader-B.attempt-N.result.json`), `prompt` (its actual prompt), `reader_report` (exact canonical `research/RUN-reader-B.md` prose report, bound by its actual raw hash; arbitrary own-run prose archives are rejected), `observed_source` (exact complete helper source), `consumer_source` (captured actual consumer source), `consumer_manifest` (captured actual owning manifest). When the manifest is archived, `consumer_manifest_original_path` is its exact canonical `research/RUN-batch-B.pages.json` origin.

The complete structured native tail must equal the entire archived findings object. Native identity, role, single covered batch, successful process and terminal completion, prompt and chronology are mandatory. Clipped tails are deliberately unsupported. The immutable indexed finding must retain its original subject label, consumer and `observed_source.snapshot: current`; the observed raw hash must exactly equal the full archived source. The historical finding is never rewritten.

Both archived and current helper have exact ID, `status:draft` and exact `pipeline_run:RUN`. During active Step 3 its current **entire bytes** must equal the observed archive: metadata or body edits fail closed and require separately authorized ordinary owner repair, not this route. All run manifests are searched for homes; any target home or duplicate consumer home rejects. The consumer must have one current home in the named batch and directly list the helper in both actual source `deps` and its manifest item's `deps`. All four archived/current source and manifest dependency fields must be arrays consisting only of valid item IDs; YAML scalar strings are rejected, even when their text contains the helper ID. The captured consumer/manifest independently bind that same direct edge. Transitive reachability, `justified_by`, aliases, a run marker alone, or guessed ownership do not qualify.

The normalized scope finding uses the honest type `unmanifested-draft-dependency`, its exact binding, and an observed hash for the exact helper archive. `reportOnlyFinding` restores the original native label when comparing against immutable native JSON. The scope adds **no** target to `manifest_post`, high-risk work, or `refuter_scope`. Collection validates this special reader context but does not pretend a native refuter read it. Order generation prints the actual read-only obligation and all limits instead of looking up a fictitious producer.

Alpha independently decides the ordinary `reader:B:N` obligation and retains `consumer_id`, one ordinary defect-ledger row, and the stamp of the actual current context carrier. The carrier binds the helper's raw and canonical hashes, owner entry, and current consumer source and manifest-item projection. Ordinary edits to the owned consumer can change its current seal while leaving the exact helper observation unchanged; removing the direct edge rejects. Alpha may not edit this context, accept it as a frontier item, accept a fatal fix, or use `context_accepted`. Only `false_positive`, `confirmed_nonfatal` or `escalated` are supported. A nonfatal decision requires `nonfatal-recorded`, not a repaired disposition. Escalation remains a normal blocker. The pre-existing evidence, ledger closure, per-obligation and final seal checks remain mandatory.

Step 3 closure freezes the registry and every exact native, historical source, consumer and manifest archive reference in its ordinary artifact map. During active Step 3 the route revalidates actual current context and edges. Once a real dependency-ordered v3 closure exists, historical verification reads only those frozen evidence files; later legitimate owner repairs do not become new Step 3 observations and are not rejected merely for changing a current context body. Ordinary closure artifact-hash comparison still rejects any registry or historical-evidence mutation.

No missing registry relaxes default behavior: the old out-of-scope diagnostic remains. No registry registration, state change, gate permission, review verdict, source edit or native decision is performed by these helpers. Root owns code integration, current module-closure resealing, actual drain/registration and normal native dispatch. Other finding classes and guards are unchanged.

Focused tests are isolated fixtures, including the actual scope lifecycle. They cover native-output/prompt tampering, missing or forged identity, edited source or run marker, invented/duplicate homes, missing direct edges, changed original finding, unsupported verdicts, missing/stale seals, ordinary consumer amendment, and historical closure versus later source repair. Run the candidate test file under `node --test` from the repository root; it overlays candidate tools into disposable fixture trees and never installs canonical code or registries.

## Native refuter extra read of the same registered direct context

The existing registry also permits an actual refuter to open and flag that exact unchanged helper as **extra read-only supplier context**, while all required assigned coverage remains owed. No registry entry, subject scope or frontier ownership is added. Flag attribution requires exactly one already registered reader context for the batch and helper ID: a refuter schema flag has no consumer field, so multiple registered consumers/observations of that ID are ambiguous and reject only when a flag needs attribution. Context discovery retains all actual reader anchors instead of rejecting ordinary collection merely because two consumer-specific reader obligations reference the same helper. The matching reader obligation must actually be present in the batch's current version-2 scope, and its named direct consumer must remain assigned there. The entire existing reader/source/manifest authority is independently revalidated.

For an extra opened registered helper, the actual original stable refuter result must be byte-identical to its immutable attempt result, successful in both process and terminal summary, have the exact role/label/single covered batch and prompt path, and contain a complete parsed structured tail equal to the entire canonical original refuter report. That report must actually open the helper once. The normalization binds its exact one-based flagged index and finding hash, canonical report raw hash, immutable attempt raw hash, prompt path/raw hash, original reader obligation and exact unchanged registered source hash. The prompt hash is a current collection-time binding; the successful result authenticates its native path, not an otherwise absent historical prompt-byte digest. Later changes invalidate the binding. No new historical refuter source-byte observation is invented: the source remains the exact unchanged reader-observed archive.

Only such a registered helper can appear as an extra flagged context. Unrelated extra suppliers retain the prior rules: a generic read may be permitted as prerequisite context but does not acquire flagged scope; unrelated foreign flags, missing assigned coverage, invalid native output or arbitrary extra reads still reject. Normalized type is `unmanifested-draft-dependency`, with the existing reader binding plus `owner_unmanifested_refuter_context`. Its `observed_sha256` matches the exact registered reader carrier so independently adjudicated reader/refuter obligations can use the ordinary same-defect sharing rules. Its current decision carrier additionally seals the complete actual refuter observation binding. No producer batch is fabricated.

Projection back to the original refuter schema strips every injected type, consumer, observed-source, authority and reader-anchor field. In particular it does **not** inject the reader's original `in-run-dependency` label into the original refuter flag, whose schema has no subject label. Both original reader and refuter obligations remain mandatory and distinct, as does every owned title flag. Alpha must independently adjudicate them all. The existing read-only verdict restriction, ordinary closed ledger, exact consumer and current seal apply to both. Sharing one nonfatal-recorded ledger row requires the existing explicit same-defect evidence and matching observed carrier; it does not discharge an omitted decision.

The existing closure-evidence helper additionally freezes every collected refuter report, immutable attempt and prompt reference from these scope bindings. Active Step 3 revalidates complete native output, exact reader authority and unchanged source. After actual sealed closure, only historical references are verified; later legitimate source repairs remain allowed and do not claim new past reading. Original reports, source, registry and native decisions are never written by this extension. It does not request a fresh native reread for a legitimate already completed supplier-context read.

Without any applicable registry context for the requested batch, refuter context discovery returns an empty map before applying version-2 anchor checks. Thus default legacy version-3 scopes and registries belonging only to other batches retain their previous behavior; an actual applicable opt-in still requires the strict version-2 reader scope.

## Separate owner-current basis when the native reader supplied no attribution/hash

An entry may explicitly set `native_finding_basis: "in-flight-null-consumer-unobserved-owner-current-context-v1"`. Unknown basis values reject; entries without this field retain every exact-observation rule above unchanged. This second basis requires the original native finding to have **exactly** `subject_type:"in-flight-item"`, `consumer_id:null`, `observed_source:null`. Do not relabel it as the reader's direct-dependency observation. The entry instead supplies `owner_context_consumer_id`, `owner_current_source` and `owner_current_review`; it must not supply `consumer_id` or `observed_source` as though native attribution existed.

All original complete native findings, exact successful attempt, prompt/canonical prose, indexed finding hash, unique owned consumer, actual direct source/manifest array edges, zero helper homes, exact run marker and read-only guards remain mandatory. The canonical native reader prose must name both helper ID and separate owner consumer witness. Both archived/current consumer source and archived/current manifest edges are checked as before. The helper's current entire bytes must equal the owner-current archive, with no assertion that these were historical native source bytes.

`owner_current_review` is a raw-bound own-run research JSON record, root-owned and explicitly completed. It requires version/run, `owner_identity:"/root"`, actual `recorded_at` no later than entry registration, `full_current_proof_read:true`, `affected_consumer_use_reviewed:true`, `source_repaired:false`, `mathematical_acceptance:false`, `native_coverage_adopted:false`, exact `obligation`, `supplier_id`, `routing_consumer_witness`, and exact raw refs `current_source`, `current_consumer`. Those refs must equal the entry's actual owner-current/helper and consumer archives. Required nonempty refs `delegated_review` and `current_provenance` remain bound separately. The root record must retain concrete `root_actual_reading`, `interface_result`, `preserved_gap`, `history` and `limits`, each at least 80 characters. This is a truthful root review/adoption, never a helper-generated claim of reading.

The bound delegated review identifies its actual `/root/…` reviewer, run, supplier, original obligation and routing consumer, completion and no repair/acceptance/coverage claims. Its `used_clause` must literally occur in the helper archive; every nonempty `consumer_premise_quotes` entry must literally occur in the assigned consumer archive. The proof and use are not certified merely by satisfying a JSON shape: actual root/delegated reading and independent native Alpha adjudication remain necessary. This route freezes actual review evidence and preserves its limitations; it cannot convert a sound first-assertion use into acceptance of an unrelated criterion gap.

In this mode the normalized finding keeps `consumer_id:null`, `observed_source:null` and `observed_sha256:null`. It separately stores the owner witness and basis. Original projection restores `in-flight-item` and both nulls exactly. The current decision carrier still binds the actual current-source/consumer/archive authority, without claiming a historical observed carrier. A decision must retain null native consumer, separate `owner_context_consumer_id`, `historical_delta_unknown:true` and explicit `owner_resolution` of at least 40 characters. Only independent nonfatal maintenance, false positive or escalation is permitted. The native severity/evidence are never silently changed. Any current helper or reviewed consumer-use source edit invalidates this route until separately authorized ordinary root review/repair and updated genuine authority; no Alpha edit permission is granted.

The exact-observation refuter-context extension above deliberately excludes this nullable basis: a refuter extra-read/flag cannot silently inherit a nonexistent historical raw observation from this new mode. It remains unassigned, read-only reader context only. There is no addition to frontier, high-risk work or refuter coverage.

Closure freezes owner-current source, root review, delegated review, current provenance and both archive refs along with the unchanged native evidence and registry. After genuine v3 closure, historical verification reads those frozen bytes only. Legitimate later repairs do not become new past observations and do not fail merely because current source differs; historical evidence mutation still rejects. No registry or review record is written by the module.

The carrier compares wrapped object values, not array values: a missing field is distinct from explicit null. Thus deleting any mandatory nullable native field rejects, and inventing null optional owner-current fields on an exact71 route also rejects.

## Multiple exact reader contexts with the same helper

Discovery may return an explicit ambiguous group containing all actual authenticated reader anchors. It does not choose a consumer, merge obligations or manufacture coverage. With no extra helper read or flag, ordinary collection proceeds unchanged. An actual extra read without a helper flag also proceeds: the existing successful exact native output/prompt and unchanged source/direct-edge guards authenticate that read, and no consumer attribution is needed. The helper remains only in `refuter_context_opened`, never `refuter_scope`. Every distinct original reader obligation still needs its own independently sealed decision and ordinary closed ledger.

The instant a schema refuter flag needs binding to that shared helper, the binder rejects an ambiguous group before any normalization. A single uniquely registered context retains the prior actual flag behavior. Unrelated extra reads/flags, missing assigned coverage, edited source, missing native evidence and invalid attribution remain rejected. This is discovery deferral only, not a new registry or verdict/repair permission.
